# Commit and push after every change

When a task has written, edited, or deleted files, commit those changes and push to the tracked remote before you stop. Do not wait for a second prompt.

## Sequence

1. Finish the work (including `architecture.md` when that rule requires it)
2. `git status`, `git diff`, and `git log -8 --oneline` so the message matches this repo
3. Stage only the files from this task. Do not stage secrets (`.env`, credentials)
4. Commit with a short message that says why
5. `git push` to the existing upstream. If the branch has no upstream, `git push -u origin HEAD`
6. Confirm with `git status` that the branch is clean and not behind

## Do not

- Empty commits
- `git commit --amend` unless the owner asked, the HEAD commit is yours, and it was not pushed
- `--no-verify`, `--force`, `push --force`, or `reset --hard`
- `git config` edits
- Interactive git (`-i`)

If commit or push fails, fix the cause and retry a new commit. Do not leave finished work only on disk.
